This product is an independent TypeScript implementation of the Verifiable Intent
specification. It is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Verifiable Intent is an open specification and reference implementation by the
agent-intent project:

  - Specification: https://verifiableintent.dev
  - Upstream repository: https://github.com/agent-intent/verifiable-intent
    (Apache License, Version 2.0)

This package is a community initiative. It is NOT an official agent-intent release
and is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the agent-intent project.
It tracks the Verifiable Intent specification and aims for byte/verdict
compatibility with the upstream reference, but any errors are our own.

Portions of the design, the credential/layer model, and the conformance test
vectors (test-vectors/vectors.json) derive from the upstream Verifiable Intent
project and remain under its Apache-2.0 license. This implementation has been
independently written for standalone TypeScript distribution: it was authored by
following the official SD-JWT specifications (IETF SD-JWT) and the Verifiable
Intent documentation, and by mirroring the upstream Python reference
implementation for byte/verdict compatibility.

Development note: this package was built with AI assistance (Claude) and reviewed
and validated by the author, a payments software engineer (@yuno).
